(:page 27 :footers ("Exploring the Moon -- A Teacher's Guide with Activities, NASA EG-1997-10-116-HQ" "17") :cells ((0 0 1 1 "Property") (0 1 1 1 "Earth") (0 2 1 1 "Moon") (0 3 1 1 "Brain Busters") (1 0 1 1 "Equatorial  diameter") (1 1 1 1 "12,756 km") (1 2 1 1 "3,476 km") (1 3 1 1 "How long would it take to drive  around the Moon's equator at  80 km per hour?") (2 0 1 1 "Surface area") (2 1 1 1 "510 million  square km") (2 2 1 1 "37.8 million  square km") (2 3 1 1 "The Moon's surface area is  similar to that of one of Earth's  continents. Which one?") (3 0 1 1 "Mass") (3 1 1 1 "5.98 x 10 24 kg") (3 2 1 1 "7.35 x 10 22 kg") (3 3 1 1 "What percentage of Earth's mass  is the Moon's mass?") (4 0 1 1 "Volume") (4 1 1 1 "---") (4 2 1 1 "---") (4 3 1 1 "Can you calculate the volumes of  Earth and the Moon?") (5 0 1 1 "Density") (5 1 1 1 "5.52 grams per  cubic cm") (5 2 1 1 "3.34 grams per  cubic cm") (5 3 1 1 "Check this by calculating the  density from the mass and  volume.") (6 0 1 1 "Surface  gravity") (6 1 1 1 "9.8 m/sec/sec") (6 2 1 1 "1.63 m/sec/sec") (6 3 1 1 "What fraction of Earth's gravity is  the Moon's gravity?") (7 0 1 1 "Crust") (7 1 1 1 "Silicate rocks.  Continents  dominated by  granites. Ocean  crust dominated  by basalt.") (7 2 1 1 "Silicate rocks.  Highlands  dominated by  feldspar-rich  rocks and maria  by basalt.") (7 3 1 1 "What portion of each body is  crust?") (8 0 1 1 "Mantle") (8 1 1 1 "Silicate rocks  dominated by  minerals  containing iron  and magnesium.") (8 2 1 1 "Similar to Earth.") (8 3 1 1 "Collect some silicate rocks and  determine the density. Is the  density greater or lesser than the  Earth/Moon's density? Why?")))
(:page 28 :footers ("18" "Exploring the Moon -- A Teacher's Guide with Activities, NASA EG-1997-10-116-HQ") :cells ((0 0 1 1 "Property") (0 1 1 1 "Earth") (0 2 1 1 "Moon") (0 3 1 1 "Brain Busters") (1 0 1 1 "Core") (1 1 1 1 "Iron, nickel metal") (1 2 1 1 "Same, but core is  much smaller") (1 3 1 1 "What portion of each body is  core?") (2 0 1 1 "Sediment or  Regolith") (2 1 1 1 "Silicon and  oxygen bound in  minerals that  contain water,  plus organic  materials.") (2 2 1 1 "Silicon and oxygen  bound in minerals,  glass produced by  meteorite impacts,  small amounts of  gases (e.g., hydrogen)  implanted by the solar  wind. No water or  organic materials.") (2 3 1 1 "Do you think life ever existed  on the Moon?  Why or why not?") (3 0 1 1 "Atmosphere  (main  constituents)") (3 1 1 1 "78 % nitrogen,  21 % oxygen") (3 2 1 1 "Basically none. Some  carbon gases (CO$_{2}$ ,  CO, and methane),  but very little of them.  Pressure is about one- trillion of Earth's  atmospheric pressure.  27.3 Earth days") (3 3 1 1 "Could you breathe the lunar  atmosphere?") (4 0 1 1 "Length of day  (sidereal  rotation  period)") (4 1 1 1 "23.93 hours") (4 2 1 1 "How long does daylight last  on the Moon?") (4 3 1 1 "Surface temperature  ranges from -193°C  (night in polar  regions) to 111°C  (day in equatorial  regions).") (5 0 1 1 "Surface  features") (5 1 1 1 "Air temperature  ranges from  -88°C (winter in  polar regions) to  58°C (summer in  tropical regions).") (5 2 1 1 "Surface temperature  ranges from -193°C  (night in polar  regions) to 111°C  (day in equatorial  regions).") (5 3 1 1 "Why are the temperatures of  Earth and the Moon so  different?") (6 0 1 1 "Surface  features") (6 1 1 1 "25 % land  (seven continents)  with varied terrain  of mountains,  plains, river valley-  leys. Ocean floor  characterized by  mountains, plains.") (6 2 1 1 "84 % heavily-cratered  highlands.  16 % basalt-covered  maria.  Impact craters-- some with bright rays,  crater chains, and  rilles.") (6 3 1 1 "Compare maps of Earth and  the Moon. Is there any  evidence that plate tectonics  operated on the Moon?")))
